    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31058" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nixŭrĭo</span></b> ,
		īre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a. desid.</i> [nixus, from nitor], <i>to wish to lean</i> or <i>rest
			upon</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nixurit qui niti vult et in conatu saepius
					aliquā re perpellitur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nigid. 144, 20</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, for parturio, <i>to
				wish to bring forth</i>: nixurio, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλοτοκέω</span>, Gloss. Philox.</div>
